- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote a test for meta.trace_id existence but the test likely accepts
    the hardcoded 'none' value. No phase flagged the hardcoded trace_id.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: 'No structured logging / tracing anywhere\
    \ \u2014 all files. Zero tracing::info!, tracing::warn!, or span instrumentation\
    \ in any handler or middleware.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged misleading SECURITY comments claiming logging exists
    when it doesn't.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test was written for non-ASCII characters in X-Tenant-ID header. Security
    edge cases covered other areas but not this specific input validation.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests checking 'no stack traces, no internal types,
    no DB details in errors' but the reviewer confirmed these only check status codes.
    No body content assertions were flagged.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote a CORS preflight test but it only checks status code/existence,
    not actual CORS headers. The reviewer flagged CORS policy being too permissive
    (I10) but not the test gap itself.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Since I4 (zero logging) was flagged but not fixed, I9 (wrong log levels
    after fixing I4) could not have been caught. No phase discussed log level differentiation
    between 4xx and 5xx.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [HIGH]: 'CORS policy is allow_origin(Any) \u2014 lib.rs:66.\
    \ Wide-open CORS means any website can make authenticated cross-origin requests...\
    \ This is CWE-942 (Permissive CORS Policy).'"
